Constraint-surfacing probes. Household example at 2026-03-31 unless a case file is named.

══ 1. Which laws govern an account? (401k: 13 laws listed, no limits, no headroom)
$ axiom why retirement -C ../../examples/02-household --today 2026-03-31
Why assets/retirement

Composition
  Holds       Quantity  Plain money  Parcels
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  USD    43,700.00 USD                     1

Parcels
  Place                   Quantity     Basis  Acquired    Tied to  From
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  assets/retirement  43,700.00 USD  0.00 USD  2025-12-31           journal/2025/12.ax:9

Governed by
  Law                            When       Governs                                                      Explains                                                                    Written
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  deferral-limit                 on in      every 401k                                                   Elective deferrals are capped for each person and calendar year, across     us/401k.ax:28
  pretax-deferral                on in      every 401k                                                   A deferral is pay you chose not to receive, so it is not taxed this year    us/401k.ax:38
  count-wages                    on in      everyone living under us, and all they own                   Wages are ordinary income (IRC §61(a)(1)). Everything that arrives from a   us.ax:58
  count-interest                 on in      everyone living under us, and all they own                   Interest is ordinary income in the year it is earned (IRC §61(a)(4)),       us.ax:66
  count-dividends                on in      everyone living under us, and all they own                   Dividends are income in the year they are paid (IRC §61(a)(7)), except      us.ax:76
  credit-withholding             on in      everyone living under us, and all they own                   Tax withheld from pay, or paid in installments, is credited against the     us.ax:108
  credit-ca-withholding          on in      everyone living under us/ca, and all they own                Tax withheld from pay, or paid in installments, is credited against the     us/ca.ax:36
  count-distributions            on gain    every 401k                                                   Money that comes out of a 401(k) is ordinary income in the year it comes    us/401k.ax:48
  early-withdrawal               on gain    every 401k                                                   Money taken out before age 59½ carries an additional 10% tax on top of      us/401k.ax:60
  count-short-term-gains         on gain    everyone living under us, and all they own                   A gain on something held for a year or less is taxed as ordinary income     us.ax:86
  count-long-term-gains          on gain    everyone living under us, and all they own                   A gain on something held for more than a year is taxed at the lower         us.ax:97
  transfer-tax                   on gain    everyone living under us/ca/san-francisco, and all they own  Selling real property in San Francisco owes the city a transfer tax on the  us/ca/san-francisco.ax:33
  required-minimum-distribution  each year  every 401k                                                   From age 73, an owner must take a minimum distribution from a 401(k)        us/401k.ax:73

