══ 3. The 401(k) deferral cap is a law: what does it say it has counted?
$ axiom why deferral-limit -C ../../examples/02-household --today 2026-03-31
Why deferral-limit

  Law       deferral-limit
  ─────────────────────────────────
  When      on in
  Governs   every 401k
  Written   us/401k.ax:28
  Ran       3 times
  Recorded  0 violations, 3 effects
  · Elective deferrals are capped for each person and calendar year, across
  · every plan they hold (IRC §402(g)), with a catch-up from age 50 and a
  · larger one from 60 through 63 (IRC §414(v)). Employer contributions do not
  · count. This payment took the year's deferrals over the cap. Ask payroll to lower the deferral.
    Any excess must also be returned
  · by the plan before April 15 of the next year, or it is taxed twice
  · (IRC §402(g)(2)).

Recent effects
  Date        Effect                  Amount  Owed to  From
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  2026-01-15  elective-deferrals  800.00 USD           journal/2026/01.ax:18
  2026-02-13  elective-deferrals  800.00 USD           journal/2026/02.ax:33
  2026-03-13  elective-deferrals  800.00 USD           journal/2026/03.ax:15
[exit status 0]

